## compiler/stage1/rt/rt_dec.src -- the decimal arithmetic trampolines written in Lume (rt_lume_dec: only a program
## that does decimal arithmetic through an untyped operand -- a parameter, a list element -- gets them; others get the
## stub rt_dec_dyn_stub in runtime_core.lume). Compiled by `lumec --raw`. They forward the two operands to the program's
## __lume_dyn_* sugar (decimal_add and friends, emitted on demand), the same role the hand-written trampolines had.
## The decimal-shape test __rt_anyd and the detection .Lrt_isd1/.Lrt_isd0 stay in runtime_core.lume (ltv_rt parses
## their spans). __rt_dcmp untags the tagged comparison word to a machine int with an arithmetic shift, as `sarq $1` did.
fn __rt_dadd(a, b) = __lume_dyn_add(a, b)
fn __rt_dsub(a, b) = __lume_dyn_sub(a, b)
fn __rt_dmul(a, b) = __lume_dyn_mul(a, b)
fn __rt_ddiv(a, b) = __lume_dyn_div(a, b)
fn __rt_dcmp(a, b) = bit_shr(__lume_dyn_cmp(a, b), 1)
